INT. BONDED WAREHOUSE - CHEESE AGING CAVE - NIGHT

Rows of wheels stacked to the ceiling. Cold. Ammonia and rind.

A woman in a hairnet, DOLORES "DOLLY" PRITCHARD-ABARA (50s), runs a finger along a shelf. She doesn't look at the two men by the door.

A man in a good suit, CASIMIR VOLKOV (40s), checks his cuffs. He is early. He hates being early.

The second man, LENNOX "LEFTY" BATISTE (30s, work gloves, one sleeve rolled), leans on a hand truck. He taps it.

She lifts a wheel. Turns it. Sniffs.

LEFTY
It's the right one.

DOLLY
We'll see.

She sets it down. Wipes her hands on her apron. He watches her hands.

A fourth figure comes down the aisle: INSPECTOR HOLLIS TANAKA-REED (50s, county badge on a belt clip). Slow. Wheezing from the cold. She stops three rows away.

HOLLIS
Evening.

Nobody answers. She nods at the shelves.

HOLLIS (CONT'D)
Lot of inventory.

DOLLY
It's a big cave.

Hollis smiles. Moves closer. Casimir shifts his weight. He glances at Lefty. Lefty looks at the floor.

HOLLIS
Mind if I look at the paperwork?

DOLLY
Back office.

HOLLIS
I'd rather look here.

She waits. Dolly hands over a clipboard. She flips pages. Doesn't read them.

HOLLIS (CONT'D)
Funny. These numbers line up exactly.

DOLLY
We keep good books.

HOLLIS
Nobody keeps books this good.

She sets the clipboard on a wheel. Casimir steps forward. Lefty's hand tightens on the truck.

A fifth voice, from the dark behind the last row.

PEPPER (O.S.)
Everybody just stay where you are.

Out of the dark: PEPPER NAKAMURA-OSEI (20s, the night cleaner, mop bucket, calm). A pistol in her yellow glove.

She points at no one in particular. At the room.

PEPPER
Mrs. Pritchard, you said you'd be gone by ten.

Dolly doesn't blink. She looks at the wheel Hollis is leaning on.

Hollis sees it. Straightens. Takes her hand off the cheese.

Lefty lets go of the hand truck. It rolls a foot. Stops.

Casimir smooths his tie.

The compressor kicks on. A long, low hum.

Pepper lowers the pistol.

PEPPER (CONT'D)
(quietly)
It's cold in here.

Dolly takes off her apron. Folds it. Sets it on the shelf. She nods once to Hollis, who nods back.

They walk out together. The two men follow. Pepper stays, looking at the wheels, the mop bucket at her feet.
